; preflight-run.fk — the runnable door for observe/preflight.fk.
;
; WHY THIS EXISTS, and it is a finding rather than a convenience.
; The practice landed in AGENTS.md as `(pf-report "path")` — an EXPRESSION.
; Asked to follow the repo's practice from a blank context, grok found it, used
; it, and reported the one thing that was missing: "How to invoke preflight as a
; one-liner is only shown as (pf-report "…"), not a full fkwu --src recipe. I
; had to write a tiny driver." Every reader was going to write that same driver,
; at exactly the moment they were already dealing with something broken. A
; practice that costs a scaffold before it can be used will be skipped when it
; is most needed.
;
; Direct-source Form does not read argv (bootstrap/ground-recursive.fk says so
; plainly), so the target arrives in a file:
;
;   echo cognition/tests/your-band.fk > /tmp/preflight-target
;   ./fkwu --src observe/preflight-run.fk
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM ONLY — preflight shells out to compare kernels.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/preflight.fk

(do
    (defn pfr-target-file () "/tmp/preflight-target")
    (defn pfr-trim-loop (s n)
        (if (le n 0) ""
            (if (str_eq (substring s (sub n 1) n) "\n") (pfr-trim-loop s (sub n 1))
                (substring s 0 n))))
    (defn pfr-target ()
        (if (eq (fs_exists (pfr-target-file)) 0) ""
            (pfr-trim-loop (read_file (pfr-target-file))
                           (str_len (read_file (pfr-target-file))))))
    (defn pfr-run ()
        (do (let t (pfr-target))
            (if (eq (str_len t) 0)
                "preflight-run: write the target path to /tmp/preflight-target first"
                (pf-report t))))
    ; PRINT IT, do not merely RETURN it — this door was mute for its whole life.
    ; Witnessed 2026-08-03: `./fkwu --src observe/preflight-run.fk` printed `5171` on a clean cell
    ; and `11846` on a cell with an unresolved call. Both are opaque handles to a string BUILT AT
    ; RUNTIME; a string LITERAL in the same position prints its text. So the trailing-value printer
    ; renders a constructed string as an integer, and the practice CLAUDE.md sends every reader to
    ; showed a number where the report should be. That is preflight's own failure mode wearing
    ; preflight's face: a green-looking number standing in for detail the reader needed, and 11846
    ; carries a CARRIED ERRORS chain while looking exactly as calm as 5171.
    ; `print_str` renders the text; the value is still returned so a caller can fold on it.
    (do (let report (pfr-run))
        (print_str report)
        0))
